Action: mass_spectrometry_spectra
Action Input: {}

Thought: The mass spectrometry data suggests a molecular ion peak at m/z 233.963, which is likely the molecular weight of the compound. To deduce the molecular formula, I will retrieve the isotopic distribution to help identify the elements present.
Action: retrieve_isotope_distribution
Action Input: {}

Thought: The isotopic distribution data can help identify the presence of elements like chlorine or bromine due to their distinct M+2 peaks. The mass spectrometry data shows a significant M+2 peak, suggesting the presence of either chlorine or bromine. I will now use the molecular weight to deduce the molecular formula and check for possible isomers.
Action: obtain_isomers_from_molecular_formula
Action Input: {"molecular_formula": "C10H8Cl2"}

Thought: I have obtained several possible isomers for the molecular formula C10H8Cl2. To identify the correct isomer, I will use the proton NMR spectra to match the chemical environment of the hydrogens in the compound.
Action: proton_nmr_spectra
Action Input: {}
